nts from regenerative  fabric we take this from warehouses it's  all waste and i already used garments  like do they just sell it in bulk yeah  so they have like tones and tones and  tones of garment when you enter into  this place you realize also  how fashion industry i've been like  producing so much the last 50 years yeah  so basically this is our past i mean  this is the past of fashion and we are  like taking piece of it um and selecting  into that to make new garments and then  no garment is the same either right  because every piece is yeah every piece  is different all of them they are unique  and the only thing that repeats is the  process of making but indeed the piece  itself like if this will be  on the back of your shirt all of the  shirt would be different right  it was marine's grandfather a collector  and second-hand dealer who first taught  her the value of vintage  looking at fashion through an ethical  and sustainable lens allowed marine to  foresee many of the issues that the  industry is only just starting to wake  up to  you know you clearly feel very deeply  about the state of the world you think  deeply about  the climate and the environment  but you're now saying you feel  optimistic  well i think before it was more about  ringing the bell alarming people  but because like in the fashion industry  no one was looking at that  and i was also working for this industry  so i do not want it to be a part of  just being there making one more skirt  you know i was hoping that maybe you  know some other people of the fashion  industry were thinking about that too we  really have to think about  yeah the environment that we are living  in and the planet that we are destroying  every day so if i'm there i have to at  least um  making a small change so what is luxury  to you and what is that luxury customer  that you are  appealing to what are they looking for i  believe that you can feel it when you  touch it i think people that are in  fashion for long they will know you know  how this thing is stitch and even if you  don't know like this old thing you will  feel it if like for me it's really  joyful when i take a cushion cover and i  can transform it into a  shirt that look cool i'm like yeah  that's nice  what is the goal of the company  i think the goal of the of the company  is to um  question  the fashion industry try to resolve some  of the questions i mean basically every  day we are doing that  and  it's to make an ecosystem  a new ecosystem um kind of exists  a fashion business does not succeed on  aesthetics alone  now more than ever those designs need to  be rooted in clear values  sustainability for me it has become a  very personal thing really just maybe  doing couture is my way taking  a minute of silence almost to reflect  this is why the show will be in full  silence  no music there will be no music the  first time i never showed my work in  silence wow  that minute of silence  is very symbolic from what i just told  you about fashion as an industry all the  white noise things that don't matter  i've seen designers injecting more of  their personal values into their designs  and asking provocative questions about  fashion and its role in the world  marine and demnar are asking how fashion  can more positively impact the people in  our communities the societies we live in  and the planet we all share  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

